From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/26] Learn fence and timeline completion from the completion
 feed

With bit 0x200 the process opens a completion feed stream and sends
COMPLETION_WATCH after every submission that signals a fence or timeline
semaphore (caboose-bounded-memory/completion_feed.h). Fence status, fence
waits, timeline values and timeline waits then resolve locally from the feed's
records, without a round trip and without holding the encoder; prefetched fence
waits are not sent. Fences and semaphores with imported or exportable payloads,
presentation-engine acquire fences and sparse binding signals are asked about
on the device stream as before.
